title: Luke
---
<<declare $helpedLuke = false>>
<<declare $lukeWillHelp = false>>


<<if $helpedLuke>>
    Luke: Thanks again for helping me!
    <<stop>>
<<endif>>

Luke: Hey! You free today? I have something big planned...
-> Yeah, I have time. <<if getBool("hasChapelPass") and hasActions()>>
    <<jump HelpLuke>>
-> No, I don't have time, sorry.
    <<jump DeclineLuke>>
===

title: HelpLuke
---
<<useAction>>
Luke: Bet! I'm throwing Grove's Perfect Party, and I need some help. You in?
-> Absolutely!
    <<jump HelpLuke2>>
-> No thanks.
    <<jump DeclineLuke>>

<<stop>>
===

title: HelpLuke2
---
Luke: Sweet! We need a few things, first, we need posters to spread the word. Grab some paper, and then meet me at class for more.
<<set $helpedLuke = true>>
<<setBool "lukePath" true>>
<<stop>>
===

title: DeclineLuke
---
Luke: No worries! I'll see you around.
<<stop>>
===

title: LukeClass
---
<<if getBool("lukePath")>>
    <<jump LukePathClass>>
<<endif>>

<<if getBool("friendedLuke")>>
    Luke: What's up man! Good to see someone with some common sense around here!
    <<stop>>
<<endif>>

Luke: Hey man, quick question. Very important for our friendship...
Luke: What's your opinion on Windows???
-> It's fine.
    <<jump LukeHatesWindows>>
-> I hate it.
    <<jump LukeYaps>>

<<stop>>
===

title: LukeHatesWindows
---
Luke: What an awful opinion, it is OBJECTIVELY worse!
Luke: Can't have someone with your mindset going around campus...
<<gameOver "Game Over! Luke REALLY hates Windows...">>

<<stop>>
===

title: LukeYaps
---
<<setBool "friendedLuke" true>>
Luke: RIGHT?! I'm litteraly doing two things that should not affect eachother AT ALL but the one says it can't run due to other programs!
Luke: I LOVE that you agree. If you catch anyone who disagrees, LET. ME. KNOW...
-> Understood.

<<stop>>
===

title: LukeLunch
---
<<if $purpleGuyDefeated>>
    Luke: That'll teach him to defend Windows!
    Luke: Anyway, what's up?
    -> Thanks for having my back!
        Luke: Of course, bro! That's what Linux users are for!
        <<stop>>
<<else>>
    Luke: What's up man?
    -> That guy over just yapped to me about how he ADORES Windows. <<if getBool("friendedLuke") and hasActions() and $seenWindowsGuy and !$lukeWillHelp>>
        <<jump LukeAngry>>
    -> Nothing much.
        <<stop>>
<<endif>>
===

title: LukeAngry
---
Luke: WHAT?! OH HECK NAH!! If ANYTHING comes up with him again I'm right behind you!
<<set $lukeWillHelp = true>>
-> Thank's boss.

<<stop>>
===

title: LukePathClass
---
<<if getInt("hasPaper") == 1>>
    Luke: Perfect, you brought the paper, too.
    Luke: I'll sketch some poster designs to help advertise this big party.
    
<<else>>
    Luke: Dang, you don't have a clean piece of paper.
    Luke: You can't even follow simple instructions, probably prefer Windows over Linux!
    <<jump LukeHatesWindows>>

<<endif>>

===
